---
import TrustPageShell from '../components/trust/TrustPageShell.astro';
import LegalTOC from '../components/trust/LegalTOC.astro';
import LegalSection from '../components/trust/LegalSection.astro';

const toc = [
  { id: 'overview', label: '1. Overview' },
  { id: 'information-collected', label: '2. Information You May Provide' },
  { id: 'how-we-use', label: '3. How We Use Information' },
  { id: 'third-party', label: '4. APIs and Third-Party Providers' },
  { id: 'local-storage', label: '5. Local Storage & Cookies' },
  { id: 'data-retention', label: '6. Data Retention & Security' },
  { id: 'children', label: '7. Children\'s Privacy' },
  { id: 'community', label: '8. Community Accounts' },
  { id: 'community-providers', label: '9. Community Service Providers' },
  { id: 'community-deletion', label: '10. Deleting Your Account' },
  { id: 'contact', label: '11. Contact & Changes' }
];
---
<TrustPageShell showCta={false}
  title="Privacy Policy | Food Nutrition Calculator"
  description="Read how Food Nutrition Calculator handles meal text, nutrition searches, server requests, third-party APIs, and privacy for calculator users."
  eyebrow="Privacy Policy"
  updatedAt="October 2026"
>
  <div class="legal-layout">
    <LegalTOC items={toc} />
    
    <div class="legal-content">
      <LegalSection id="overview" heading="1. Overview">
        <p>This page is provided for transparency and general information regarding how the Food Nutrition Calculator operates. The calculators work without an account or invasive tracking. If you choose to join our community, the sections below explain what we collect for that.</p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection id="information-collected" heading="2. Information You May Provide">
        <p>While using our tools, you may voluntarily input information into our calculators, such as:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Food search queries (e.g., "apple", "chicken breast").</li>
          <li>Recipe ingredient text or meal descriptions.</li>
          <li>Quantities, weights, and serving size inputs.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Additionally, standard browser and device request data (such as IP address and user-agent strings) are normally sent with web requests to our hosting servers.</p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection id="how-we-use" heading="3. How We Use Information">
        <p>The text and inputs you provide are used strictly to operate the calculators. This includes:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Returning relevant food search results.</li>
          <li>Parsing meal or recipe text (if AI parsing features are utilized).</li>
          <li>Calculating deterministic nutrition estimates based on your inputs.</li>
          <li>Improving page functionality and resolving application errors locally.</li>
        </ul>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection id="third-party" heading="4. APIs and Third-Party Providers">
        <p>To provide high-quality nutrition data and intelligent parsing, your inputs may be processed by server-side endpoints and third-party providers when configured:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>USDA FoodData Central:</strong> Search queries may be routed to USDA APIs to fetch verified nutrition data.</li>
          <li><strong>LLM Providers:</strong> If you use our natural language recipe or meal parsers, the unstructured text you enter is sent to a configured Large Language Model provider to interpret the text into structured food requests.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not expose our internal API keys to the client. However, you should assume that text entered into the natural language parser is processed by these third-party services in order to function.</p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection id="local-storage" heading="5. Local Storage & Cookies">
        <p>The calculators do not require an account. We do not use cookies for advertising, marketing, or user profiling; the only cookie we set is the sign-in cookie for community members (see section 8).</p>
        <p>Some browser storage (like <code>localStorage</code> or <code>sessionStorage</code>) may be utilized temporarily to maintain basic interface state (such as keeping a modal open or remembering a selected unit metric) while you actively use the tools.</p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection id="data-retention" heading="6. Data Retention & Security">
        <p>The calculators do not keep a saved history. Community content is kept as described in sections 8 to 10. We do not intentionally store your meal calculations or recipe histories in a long-term user database.</p>
        <p>Standard server logs may exist depending on our hosting provider's default infrastructure (e.g., Vercel, Netlify). API keys and application secrets are secured server-side. While we use modern web practices, no system is perfectly secure.</p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection id="children" heading="7. Children's Privacy">
        <p>This site is intended for general audiences. It is not directed at, nor do we knowingly collect personal data from, children under the age of 13.</p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection id="community" heading="8. Community Accounts">
        <p>Creating a community account is optional. You must be at least 18 years old to create one. If you do, we store:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Your email address and either a hashed (never plain-text) password or your Google account identifier.</li>
          <li>A public username you choose. This is the only thing other people see about you: we never show your email address or real name.</li>
          <li>What you post: posts, replies, upvotes, any photos you upload, reports you send, and private messages to the owner.</li>
          <li>A sign-in cookie that keeps you logged in. It is strictly necessary for the account to work and is not used for advertising.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Posts, replies and approved photos are public and may be seen and indexed by search engines (except in the website feedback topic). By posting you give us a non-exclusive licence to store and display your content on this site. You keep ownership of it. Please do not post personal information about yourself or anyone else, and do not upload photos of other people without their permission.</p>
        <p>If you sign in with Google, we receive your email address and a Google account identifier. We do not store your Google name or profile picture.</p>
        <p>Each account has a single-use code for the Bhaskar app. When someone redeems a code, we record only that it was used and when.</p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection id="community-providers" heading="9. Community Service Providers">
        <p>To run the community we use these providers, which process data on our behalf:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Cloudflare:</strong> hosts the site, stores account and post data in Cloudflare D1, stores photos in Cloudflare R2, and provides Turnstile, a bot check shown when you sign up or post. Turnstile may process your IP address and browser signals.</li>
          <li><strong>Resend:</strong> sends our account emails (email verification and password reset) to your address.</li>
          <li><strong>Google:</strong> only if you choose to sign in with Google.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>These providers may process data in the United States and other countries. We do not sell your data or use it for advertising.</p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection id="community-deletion" heading="10. Deleting Your Account">
        <p>You can delete your account at any time from the Your account page. Deleting it permanently removes your account, posts, replies, upvotes, photos and messages to the owner, and your Bhaskar code stops working. This cannot be undone. Content you posted that others replied to is removed with the post. Copies may remain in backups or search engine caches for a short time.</p>
        <p>You can report a post or reply you believe breaks the rules, and ask the owner for any other data request by email.</p>
      </LegalSection>

      <LegalSection id="contact" heading="11. Contact & Changes">
        <p>This policy is a practical informational template and may be updated periodically to reflect new features or architectural changes to the tools.</p>
        <p><em>Contact information may be added later as the project develops a formal support infrastructure.</em></p>
      </LegalSection>
    </div>
  </div>
</TrustPageShell>
